;; TEST-EXPECT: PASS
;; TEST-WITH[--hardware-profile=h100 --ir-target=ptx]
;; SKIP-DEFAULT-PASS
;; TEST-HOIST[CUDA]: validate-cuda-host-run
;; HOIST-HARDWARE-PROFILE: h100
;; HOIST-EXPECT: BUFFER out: 2016 1 2 3
;; SKIP-WITH[--differentiate]: "forward contention only; the + VJP is measured on the BMG side (spec 37)"
;;
;; !!! NEVER EXECUTED YET.  Written 2026-09-22; no NVIDIA box was available.  VALIDATE THIS
;; !!! FIRST on the next pod run, before reading any failure here as a compiler defect.  An
;; !!! unrun directive is a guess -- 173 spec 12 carried one that turned out to be
;; !!! unexpressible by the harness (BUG 067), which is what this warning exists to prevent.
;;
;; ENDEAVOUR 175 -- atomic-binop! under contention, on NVIDIA.  CUDA twin of spec 35.
;;
;; 64 threads hammer ONE address, so 0+1+...+63 = 2016 and the retry path is genuinely exercised
;; rather than incidentally touched.  This is the spec that puts the DERIVED BOUND under test on
;; this backend: a CAS fails only because another thread's succeeded, so (contenders) attempts
;; always suffice, and the loop uses global_size + 1.
;;
;; A lost update would read as a specific shortfall -- 1998, say -- with nothing to say why, which
;; is precisely why the construct asserts on exhaustion instead of falling out quietly.  If that
;; assert fires here but not on BMG, the bound's reasoning is wrong about NVIDIA scheduling, and
;; that finding would justify the rental on its own.
;;
;; WHY THIS NUMBER MATCHES THE BMG TWIN'S, and is not a copy-paste slip: the total is a sum over
;; ALL THREADS, so it does not depend on how threads group into warps.  Only an expectation
;; built from a PER-WARP quantity changes with the warp width -- see spec 49, where 30720
;; becomes 126976 because a 32-lane warp sums to 496 rather than 120.  Classifying each number
;; as per-thread or per-warp was the actual work in porting this set.

(def-type vec-t (vector float :address-space :global :align :compact))

(def-kernel binop_contention (&out out)
  (declare #'(&out vec-t => nil)
           (global-size :set-to 64)
           (local-size  :set-to 64))
  (let ((contrib (to-float (get-local-linear-id))))
    (atomic-binop! (~ out 0) #'+ contrib)))
